  <data name="HybridPM_Help_Needed" xml:space="preserve"><value>This CPU has performance and efficiency cores (12th-14th gen Core): without HybridPM.kext macOS holds them back, which makes the GPU look slow too. Stage 4 adds it below Lilu.kext.</value></data>
  <data name="HybridPM_Help_NotNeeded" xml:space="preserve"><value>Core Ultra, CPUs without E-cores and older CPUs do not need it.</value></data>
  <data name="Board_Help" xml:space="preserve"><value>Any board OpenCore supports: only the ACPI path of the card's slot matters, and stage 4 adapts the table to it.</value></data>
  <data name="Firmware_Uefi" xml:space="preserve"><value>UEFI</value></data>
  <data name="Firmware_Legacy" xml:space="preserve"><value>Legacy BIOS (CSM)</value></data>
  <data name="Firmware_Help_Legacy" xml:space="preserve"><value>OpenCore needs UEFI with CSM off (and Above 4G decoding and Resizable BAR on); this Windows started in legacy mode.</value></data>
  <data name="SecureBoot_Help_On" xml:space="preserve"><value>OpenCore does not start while Secure Boot is on, unless you signed it yourself: turn it off in the BIOS, as Dortania's guide does. Windows keeps working without it.</value></data>
  <data name="SecureBoot_NotSupported" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not available (legacy BIOS)</value></data>
